1
00:00:00,900 --> 00:00:08,200
That was leaving properly. Readmission is the other end: coming back from an approved leave.

2
00:00:09,199 --> 00:00:20,400
I sign in as Therese Lacson, who is already on an approved leave.

3
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:34,899
Her Readmission page says she is on leave and that enrollment stays closed until a readmission is approved. The leave she is ending is filled in for her.

4
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:44,699
The rule behind this page: a returning student writes an intent to enroll, from the Handbook, page fifty-three.

5
00:00:53,799 --> 00:01:01,799
She picks the semester she wants to return in, explains why she is ready, and confirms the four checklist items.

6
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:09,200
Again, a summary to check before sending.

7
00:01:09,400 --> 00:01:18,500
Submitted, with a four-step tracker: staff review, Dean decision, and back in the program.

8
00:01:18,700 --> 00:01:25,099
Staff side again.

9
00:01:29,099 --> 00:01:36,299
The Readmission board: the same board, with its own columns. Therese's card is in Submitted.

10
00:01:39,400 --> 00:01:43,200
I drag it to In staff review.

11
00:01:45,099 --> 00:01:52,500
The request shows the return semester, her intention, and the linked leave of absence.

12
00:01:52,700 --> 00:02:06,500
The return checklist shows what the student ticked, not yet verified by staff. Below, her history: one year in the program and two of four leave semesters already used.

13
00:02:06,700 --> 00:02:19,100
The policy check flags one thing: she wants to return before her leave ends. That is allowed only if the Dean agrees, so it says Needs review.

14
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:39,500
When I forward, I tick the checklist items I verified myself. Anything I leave unticked reaches the Dean as Needs review.

15
00:02:39,699 --> 00:02:44,400
Forwarded, and locked: waiting for the Dean.

16
00:02:44,599 --> 00:02:50,900
The Dean decides.

17
00:02:56,199 --> 00:03:08,700
The Dean finds Therese's request in With the Dean.

18
00:03:08,900 --> 00:03:18,300
The Dean drags it to Approved, back in the program, with a note.

19
00:03:18,500 --> 00:03:29,600
She is active again. Note that readmission restores her standing; it does not enroll her in subjects. That is the Academic Coordinator's next step.

20
00:03:30,800 --> 00:03:42,400
Staff side again.

21
00:03:42,599 --> 00:03:53,500
On the staff board, the card now says the next owner is the Academic Coordinator, and it is flagged for the Registrar.

22
00:03:53,699 --> 00:04:00,900
The Registrar list works exactly as before: download, send it yourself, mark sent, mark acknowledged.

23
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:16,300
I sign in as Therese Lacson, who is already on an approved leave.

24
00:04:16,500 --> 00:04:24,400
And Therese sees her readmission approved, with the messages from staff and the Dean.
